  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nHigh pressure centered over the region will bring mainly clear \nskies and cool temperatures tonight into Sun morning. Lows will \nbe mainly in the 20s across much of the area. After a cool \nstart, temperatures will warm to slightly above normal levels \nSun P.M. as high pressure shifts south of the area and a SW flow\ndevelops. The high looks to be positioned over the mid Atlantic\nregion through early next week, with ridging extending north \ninto our area providing continued dry conditions. A warm front \nmay bring a few light showers to the Adirondacks Tue P.M, but \nmost areas will remain dry. High confidence in above normal \ntemperatures persisting through next week. The next chance of \nrain arrives later next week Thu/Fri, although confidence in \ntiming and rainfall amounts is low due to considerable spread in \nguidance with regards to the pattern evolution of a potential \nclosed low or a more progressive open wave trough aloft and \nassociated cold front passage. Given high uncertainty this far \nout, 50-60% PoPs look reasonable during this time.",
